> the anchored ^warning:/^note: filter above is defense in depth; the parser below is the primary defense

After this change there **is no filter above** — `remoteRefLines`/`remoteBranchSha` feed raw `cleanCommandOutput` captures straight into the strict ref-line regex, which is now the *only* defense on the probe path. A future maintainer auditing the gh-912 fix will credit a defense layer that no longer exists and may safely skip re-checking it when touching `cleanCommandOutput`.

Two ways to fix:

